{
  "Assessment": "Patient reports a shift in work-related stress following a meeting where he was informed about a job reorganization and the subsequent layoffs. He described the meeting and the subsequent conversation with his team in detail, expressing concern about the six weeks in a sling following surgery. Patient reports no change in sleep patterns and thought records show two out of seven entries. In the room, patient engaged in conversation with more frequency than usual, with no tears observed and phone checking performed twice, which is outside of his usual behavior.",
  "Objective": "Patient reports a job reorganization involving a reduction from nine to six team members, with two hires being let go. Patient described the meeting and the subsequent team discussion in detail. Patient reports no change in sleep patterns. Patient reports thought records show two out of seven entries. In the room, patient engaged in conversation with more frequency than usual, with no tears observed and phone checking performed twice, which is outside of usual behavior.",
  "Plan": "Continue weekly sessions. Patient will be asked by the surgeon how long before he can drive. Patient will continue to attend the bereavement group.",
  "Subjective": "Patient reports the first half of the session was focused on the job reorganization, where his team went from nine to six members, and two hires were let go. He described the meeting and the subsequent conversation with his team in detail, stating he is fine and that he just keeps replaying it. Patient reports no change in sleep patterns. Patient reports thought records show two out of seven entries. Patient reports that the second half of the session was about his shoulder, with an MRI showing a tear and surgery scheduled for November. He is worried about the six weeks in a sling and asked about whether he should inform work about the surgery now or after November. Patient said it's his call and we discussed both sides. Patient did not connect the two topics and neither did the therapist."
}

